<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Black outline around the flight-screen mini-map. Specification §4.9.

     WHY: the map sits over live video with no panel behind it, the same as the HUD readouts
     since the translucent blocks were removed. Its own tiles are pale — a road layer over a
     light background — so its EDGE disappears against a bright scene exactly as the white text
     did, and the map stops reading as a distinct instrument.

     WHY THE SAME WEIGHT AS THE TEXT: hud_text_outline_width is the one per-device value the
     whole HUD uses for its edge, so the map, the readouts and the EV slider carry a single
     treatment rather than three values that drift apart.

     This is the FOREGROUND of the map container, not of the map view itself. The container is
     what the size toggle resizes, thus the outline follows the map to its expanded size with no
     second value. A GradientDrawable stroke is inset by half its width inside the bounds, so
     unlike a Canvas stroke on text it cannot be clipped by the view edge.

     ⚠ THE CORNER MUST MATCH THE CONTAINER'S CLIP, AND THAT CLIP IS NOT THIS RADIUS. A stroke is
     centred on a path inset by half its width, so the OUTER edge this frame presents has radius
     (hud_pill_radius + stroke/2). The activity clips at (hud_pill_radius + stroke), putting the
     map's cut edge on the MIDDLE of this stroke, because clipping at the bare 8dp leaves a
     sliver of map outside the border on every corner.

     ⚠ WIDENING THIS TO CHASE THE LAST OF THAT SEAM WAS TRIED AND REJECTED ON THE SIBLING
     (operator, 2026-09-12): "close enough ... dont thicken it up". A hair of pale map can still
     be found at a corner under magnification. One HUD edge weight is worth more than a perfect
     corner. Do not give this frame its own width. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">

    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />

    <corners android:radius="@dimen/hud_pill_radius" />

    <stroke
        android:width="@dimen/hud_text_outline_width"
        android:color="@color/tp_hud_outline" />
</shape>
